  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Saturday)\nIssued at 622 PM CST SUN NOV 22 2026\n\nSkies were slow to clear this afternoon, but there is now a well-\ndefined clearing line on satellite moving east of I-65. This \nlate-clearing setup means there is still plenty of moisture near \nthe ground. With calm winds ahead of the front, this will be a \nfavorable setup for fog development, especially across the \nsoutheast half of the area. Will need to monitor for the potential\nneed for a dense fog advisory.\n\n32/JDavis\n\nMoisture return ahead of an approaching cold front will be very \nlimited, with the cold front beginning to take a more E/W shape \ndue to the upper-level support. Because of the cold front \norientation, and lack of moisture, rain probabilities will be best\nin our NW zones Sunday night. Additional shower development is \npossible during the day on Monday south of I-20, but confidence is\nhigh that any additional shower activity won't amount to \nsignificant measurable rainfall. This first cold front should push\nthrough the region during the day on Monday, stalling near the \ncoast by Tuesday. Temperatures will drop slightly behind this \nfront, as colder air filters down the Appalachian mountains under \na CAD wedge. A much stronger system will begin to take shape to \nour west during this same timeframe, as a trough moving through \nthe Plains becomes cut off from the main upper-level flow. This \nclosed low is expected to work through the region on Wednesday, \nwith increased forcing and moisture resulting in some of the \nhigher rain chances we've recently seen. Widespread rainfall \nshould begin by Wednesday morning, continuing throughout the day \nand into the overnight hours. Most locations will generally see \nbetween a half an inch, and one inch of rainfall, before this \nclosed low exits the region into Thanksgiving proper. Some \nlingering showers are possible north of I-20 into Thursday, but \nmost locations are expected to remain dry for Thanksgiving Day. \nWith that being said, much colder temperatures are expected behind\nthis closed low, with seasonable to slightly below seasonable \ntemperatures remaining in place into next week.\n\n/44/",
